# 2026-09-25 17:58:05.661043
+Implement the empty VRCameraHeightSmoother MonoBehaviour. It goes on the VR camera rig, which is a child of the kart, and low-pass filters the kart's vertical (world Y) movement so suspension jitter doesn't shake the player's head. Keep namespace and class name. Implement exactly:
+- Fields: [SerializeField] private Transform followTarget; (tooltip: the kart; defaults to parent if null), [SerializeField] private float smoothTime = 0.12f; [SerializeField] private float maxOffset = 0.1f; (tooltip: max vertical metres the rig may lag behind the kart).
+- Private fields: Vector3 _baseLocalPosition; float _smoothedY; float _velocity;
+- Awake(): if followTarget is null, set it to transform.parent. Store _baseLocalPosition = transform.localPosition. If followTarget not null, _smoothedY = followTarget.position.y.
+- LateUpdate(): return if followTarget is null. float targetY = followTarget.position.y; _smoothedY = Mathf.SmoothDamp(_smoothedY, targetY, ref _velocity, smoothTime); float offset = Mathf.Clamp(_smoothedY - targetY, -maxOffset, maxOffset); _smoothedY = targetY + offset; then transform.localPosition = _baseLocalPosition; transform.position += Vector3.up * offset;
+- OnDisable(): restore transform.localPosition = _baseLocalPosition.
+Add a short XML summary comment on the class. No other files.
